   mmoouusseeiinntteerrvvaall
       The  mmoouusseeiinntteerrvvaall  function  sets  the maximum time (in thousands of a
       second) that can elapse between press and release events for them to be
       resolved  as  a _c_l_i_c_k.  An application might interpret button press and
       release events separated by more than the mouse  interval  as  a  “long
